        "gg-mpw0vwQE_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/6_edbb4fbf-f57b-4c4c-8e6c-24d9b1aa091e.png",
        "gg-mpw0vwQE_srcSet_mobile_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/6_edbb4fbf-f57b-4c4c-8e6c-24d9b1aa091e.png",
        "gg0wZ499PHU_text": "By Dr. James Caldwell / <span style=\"color:#62638E;\">Testosterone Specialist&nbsp;</span>",
        "gg41GfpX_bz_text": "<p>Reserve a Sproutly Pouch</p>",
        "gg5CwhWqvad_text": "<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:17pt;\"><strong>The Thing You Drink To Feel Sharper Is Quietly Destroying Your Cortisol&nbsp;</strong></span>",
        "gg7A0SNloWD_text": "<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:23pt;\"><strong>Men Over 35: The Real Reason You Can'tLast Longer Then 3 Minutes&nbsp;</strong></span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:20px;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span><br><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:18px;\"><strong>( the Morning Ritual That's Causing It)</strong></span>",
        "ggNKqQ5JGd8_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/Gemini_Generated_Image_96k4sn96k4sn96k4.png",
        "ggOovp2jBmw_text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong>Researchers spent years studying testosterone decline in men who were technically healthy</strong>.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">Normal sleep. Normal diet.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">Testosterone levels that looked fine on paper.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">But every symptom of low T was there. The rushed feeling. The disconnection. The lack of control that arrived like clockwork.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">They controlled for stress. They controlled for sleep quality. They even controlled for relationship satisfaction.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">The variable that kept surfacing wasn't what these men were doing wrong in the moment.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">It was what they were doing every morning without questioning it.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">In a 2019 study published in [Journal], researchers tracked men's hormone levels across different caffeine intake patterns.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong>What they found was stark: </strong>higher caffeine consumption was associated with significantly elevated cortisol levels and measurably lower free testosterone.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">Not total T. Free T. The testosterone that governs control, stamina, and staying present.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">And here's the mechanism most men never see.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong>Caffeine from regular coffee triggers a cortisol spike within 30 minutes.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">That cortisol elevation suppresses your HPG axis — the hormonal signal chain responsible for testosterone production.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">Chronic cortisol elevation directly interferes with luteinizing hormone secretion, the upstream trigger your body needs to produce testosterone.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\"><strong>Less signal = less control. More anxiety = more overthinking. More overthinking = finishing faster.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">You're in a loop. And every cup deepens it.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">&nbsp;</span></p>",
